  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustaining Our Oceans: Building healthy relationships with oceans in South-East Asia through Education for Sustainable Development (ESD)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to build healthy relationship with ocean through Education for Sustainable Development (ESD) in three countries of South-East Asia so that the children and young people who will pave the way to the future can grow up to become sustainability leaders. The project contributes to reducing ocean garbage in South-East Asian countries by educating children the negative impacts that marine litter have in their environment, including in UNESCO designated sites, and by increasing capacities of teachers and students in marine conservation.</narrative>
  </description>
